; RockCluster3 — one of 4 Rock terrain cluster variants (D-42 model_scenes variety pass).
; A mossy-anchored cluster: 1x RockMediumMoss.glb ("Rock Medium" by Quaternius, CC0,
; poly.pizza — see project/attribution/sources/quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres) as the
; larger anchor piece, plus 2x the small Rock_2.glb (same source as RockCluster2) for the
; "several rocks" read.
;
; RockMediumMoss raw measured AABB is LARGE (footprint 3.23x2.99, height 2.26 tile-units —
; modeled at a different unit scale than the other pieces, unrelated to being a "big"
; rock in-fiction) — scaled down hard (0.124x) to a ~0.28-tall anchor, comparable to
; RockCluster1's pieces, not a return to the old giant-rock problem. FLAG FOR HUMAN
; SIGN-OFF: scale and the mossy-vs-plain slab tint are first-pass judgment calls.
;
; Slab uses a mossier grey-green tint (Color(0.48, 0.52, 0.42, 1)) instead of the plain
; Rock grey, to read as a moss-touched cluster rather than a color-identical repaint of
; the other 3 variants — a deliberate per-variant differentiation, not required by schema
; (pick_variant() only needs distinct model_scenes entries, not distinct slab colors).
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap) — same fix,
; same reasoning as CommonTree1.tscn's header. X/Z only, Y (0.2) untouched.
